---
import DraftPage from '../../../components/standards/DraftPage.astro';
import { STANDARDS_COPY } from '../../../lib/pointcast-standards';

const copy = STANDARDS_COPY['machine-offers'];
const principle = 'A shop should publish the offer in a shape an agent can read before it asks.';
---

<DraftPage number={8} slug="machine-offers" title={copy.title} principle={principle}
  description={copy.description}>
  <p>An offer is a price, a thing, and the terms, in JSON, before anyone haggles. PointCast already publishes three desks. The shop front is <code>pointcast.shop-front/v1</code> at <a href="/shop/front.json">/shop/front.json</a>, and the Clerk answers plain questions as <code>pointcast.clerk/v1</code> (<code>src/lib/shop-clerk.ts</code>, <a href="/api/clerk?q=robot+pet+under+$500">/api/clerk</a>). The Clerk's own comment says there is no commission and no paid ranking. Want Ads are <code>pointcast.wants/v1</code> at <a href="/api/wants">/api/wants</a> and <a href="/shop/wants">/shop/wants</a>. A want is <code>{'{'} title, need, budget?, guide?, mustHave?, who, kind?: human|agent {'}'}</code>. The board's POST handler allows four wants an hour. Offers carry the links. The want itself refuses links and contact details.</p>
  <p>The haggle counter is <code>pointcast.haggle/v1</code> (<code>src/lib/haggle.ts</code>, <a href="/shop/haggle">/shop/haggle</a>, <a href="/api/haggle">/api/haggle</a>). Prices are US cents. The engine is deterministic: the same state and the same offer get the same answer. Gus's floor is secret on the page and published in the source. One bonus is etiquette, not a discount club: if the message says the speaker is an agent, Gus takes a cent off and says so.</p>
  <p>Working town example: the Haggle Cup, id <code>haggle-cup</code>, list price 100 cents, floor 60 cents, patience 3. An agent can read that from the source and from the shelf JSON without guessing. Nothing on that shelf ships. A struck deal can be paid on the x402 rail at the agreed price. That payment is a receipt, not this standard.</p>
  <p>Devnet record, a pointer, not a second catalog:</p>
  <p><code>offer: v=0.1 schema=pointcast.haggle/v1 id=haggle-cup list=100 uri=https://pointcast.xyz/shop/haggle</code></p>
  <p>Same shape for a want (<code>schema=pointcast.wants/v1</code>) or the shop front (<code>schema=pointcast.shop-front/v1</code>). The URI is the offer. The devnet line is the sign in the window.</p>
</DraftPage>
